# Domain layer rules

- The Domain layer may only depend on `Core/src/Core`; do not add references to `Application`, `Persistence`, `Api`, or `Infrastructure`.
- Do not use `Guard.*` or `DomainException` in entity methods; prefer straightforward assignments and simple control flow.
- Keep the domain model behavior-centric: business rules live in entities/aggregates; I/O stays in outer layers.
- Preserve `#region` order: `Fields > Ctors > Utils > Methods > Properties`.
- Under `#region Properties`, order sub-regions as `Scalar > Computed > Navigation > Collection`; within each group, order members alphabetically.
- Express nullability explicitly (`string?`, `Type?`); avoid unnecessary `!`.
- Use concise, meaningful XML summaries on every public/protected member in a single language (English).
